  "analytical_proof": {
    "schema": 1,
    "kind": "DENSE_FULL_HISTORY_UNBOUNDED_CURRENT_INSERTION_DOMAIN_ADDENDUM_NOT_GLOBAL_COMMUTATOR",
    "frozen_parent_proof": "electric_history_proof_20261011.json@088b0a77954cd0d347ce264b50e0a155c768d25bcbcc40343b808a2a5406bf40",
    "governor": "issue-222-induced-photon-delta13-continuation-20261008@52ef5afc3c8cd3c8c16ff3a0fc5e358631be5219426c2b2f246a1e7b087cd9bf",
    "precision": "Strengthens the insertion_domains clause of the frozen proof. Its sentence saying that an unbounded current operator on history vectors requires additional construction is paid HERE on the dense FULL history polynomial domain, not on every Hilbert vector. Frozen proof/actual1 bytes and claims remain immutable.",
    "native_tail_calculation": "Fix closed local h, T=sum_K s_x, m=|K|, tau=min_K theta>0, C1_h=||h||1*C_e. For EVERY finite full-history word psi_N=rho_N(p)Omega_N, q_Q(psi_N)<=b_p, ||psi_N||<=n_p, T^2<=m sum_K s_x^2 and Q>=(lambda/2)tau sum_K s_x^2. Thus ||(J_h-J_h,M)psi_N||^2<=C1_h^2 <psi_N,T 1_(T>M)psi_N><=C1_h^2*2m*b_p/(lambda tau M). This is an actual N-uniform per-word cutoff tail. It uses the paid Q propagation/insertion budget, not ground-only radial tails. Coefficients depend on the actual history word and fixed weight-centre distance.",
    "current_norm": "Cauchy gives <psi_N,T psi_N><=n_p sqrt(2m*b_p/(lambda tau)), hence ||J_h psi_N||^2<=C1_h^2 n_p sqrt(2m*b_p/(lambda tau)). A simpler sufficient bound is ||J_h psi_N||<=C1_h*(2m/(lambda tau))^(1/4)*sqrt(b_p), because Q>=1 implies n_p<=sqrt(b_p). These are Hilbert-norm insertion estimates, not graph estimates for L J_h psi_N.",
    "limiting_operator": "Each selfadjoint bounded J_h,M is already a physical each-number-preserving smooth cutoff multiplier in the SAME history left action. For every dense history polynomial [p], full-word Gram convergence and the displayed N-uniform tail make pi(J_h,M)[p] Cauchy. Define J_h^core[p]=lim_M pi(J_h,M)[p]. If [p]=0, each cutoff image is0 by bounded null-ideal preservation, hence so is the limit; representation independence is exact. Finite sums are controlled by Minkowski sums of sqrt(b_p). For any dense p,q, <[p],J_h^core[q]>=lim_M<[p],pi(J_h,M)[q]>=lim_M<pi(J_h,M)[p],[q]>=<J_h^core[p],[q]>. Therefore J_h^core is densely defined symmetric and CLOSABLE; denote its closure J_h. No essential selfadjointness or maximal multiplication domain is asserted. D(J_h) contains EVERY dense history word. Its vacuum is exactly the J_h Omega already used in the frozen same-L graph join.",
    "products_covariance": "Fixed-M current letters and all their finite history products remain in D(L) by accepted insertion graph recursion. Uncut J_h^core preserves a Hilbert-vector domain on dense words but need not map them back to that polynomial domain or D(L). Time-translated cutoff currents have limits on dense words: conjugate V(t)pi(J_h,M)V(-t), since V(-t)[p] is again a dense full-history word with paid b_(shift_-t p). Their closures obey J_h(t)=V(t)J_h V(-t) on V(t)D(J_h); likewise spatial translates. This is same-history covariance, not a global [L,E_h]=iJ_h operator identity or a static-space automorphism.",
    "nonclaims": [
      "J_h Omega in D(L) or D(E_h)",
      "every Hilbert vector in D(J_h)",
      "J_h selfadjoint rather than merely closed symmetric",
      "global common invariant E/J/L operator core",
      "small Q-form errors imply small L-graph errors",
      "actual physical ground or phase characterization",
      "IR atom or photon"
    ],
    "new_consumer": "electric_history_domain_consumer_20261011.py calculates exact native all65 C_e, B0 and weighted per-word current cutoff costs including nonzero symbolic propagation factors, evaluates cutoff thresholds for requested error squared, and checks a non-native unbounded-current full-word shift witness. This is not a native ground measurement."
  },
